gxi(){return"Help"},
gD9(){return"Help"},
gCO(){return"Privacy and data encryption"},
gCN(){return"Patient data is sensitive data. For that reason, everything uploaded to the cloud (records, surgeries and settings) is encrypted ON YOUR DEVICE with AES-256 before being sent; only encrypted data is stored on the server. Data is also always kept on your device, so the app works offline. Cloud sync requires signing in."},
gD1(){return"Patient records"},
gD2(){return"The patient list is on the left, with dynamic search on top. \u201cNew\u201d creates a record (saving the previous one). The record has the main sheet (General data, with insurance as an editable list, children and their names, spouse, city and allergies), the Obstetrics group (Obstetrics, Ultrasounds and Laboratory, one per pregnancy, separated by event; each with its own LMP and can be closed when finished, never deleted) and the Gynecology group (general visits and, separately, Studies: gynecological ultrasound, pap smear, mammography, etc., each with its type chosen from an editable list, date and result). Everything is saved with the save button, when switching patients, when closing the record and when leaving the app. Obstetrics shows reminders by pregnancy week or month of the year (Tdap, vitamins, Anti D for Rh negative and group B strep culture come predefined, and you can add your own, permanent for all records or just for one); edit them from Settings. They disappear when the corresponding box is checked. It also warns when the patient\u2019s birthday is less than a month away."},
gD7(){return"Ultrasounds and calculations"},
gD8(){return"The first ultrasound entered is the reference for the weeks calculation (weeks.days format, e.g. 12.3). The dates on which 37 to 42 weeks are reached are shown above, and there are calculators for dates and weeks. The physical exam also calculates weeks by LMP (each pregnancy has its own)."},
gCT(){return"Laboratory and template"},
gCU(){return'Each laboratory study is a column with its own date. With "Edit template" you can add your own fields, reorder them by dragging, insert separators and delete. The edited template applies to all patients and syncs across your devices.'},
gD_(){return"Printing and prescription pad"},
gD0(){return"The Print module generates A5 PDFs on your prescription pad: prescriptions, laboratory and study orders (with their own editable template and separators, like in the record; if the order doesn't fit on one sheet, it automatically continues on a second one), certificates, schedules and documents. Certificates and documents can be saved by name for reuse. The pad is customized in \u201cConfigure prescription pad\u201d, with a floating panel you can drag around to compare against the live preview: the doctor's name and titles with their own size (up to 40), color, bold, italic and a choice of typefaces (calligraphic and formal serif) besides the system default, plus an optional watermark. If the pad doesn't have the doctor's name set yet, printing opens the configuration automatically."},
gCR(){return"Settings"},
gCS(){return"In \u201cSettings\u201d you can set the language, customize the prescription pad, show or hide the help texts in the record, and manage reminders: some come predefined (Tdap, vitamins, Anti D, group B strep) which you can edit or delete, and you can add your own by pregnancy week or month of the year."},
gCY(){return"License and subscription"},
gCZ(){return"Dextor has a one-month free trial from account creation, available on the web and desktop versions (never in the cloud: the trial is always local only). After that month, a license is required: a subscription (monthly or yearly, with cloud sync, valid on web, desktop and mobile) or a one-time local payment (desktop version only, no cloud). Payment is always made on the website, via PayPal \u2014 the app itself never sells anything. The mobile version is exclusive to accounts with an active subscription; if it doesn't have one, it shows how to confirm or buy it on the website."},
gCP(){return"Backup"},
gCQ(){return"Export all your data (records, surgeries and settings) to a file, and restore it later on the same device or another one. When restoring, the data is merged with what's already there, always keeping the most recent version of each record: nothing is ever deleted."},
gD3(){return"Surgery log"},
gD4(){return"Monthly log of procedures (patient, date, insurance, procedure, role). Printing generates an A4 PDF with each insurer on separate pages, ordered by date, ready to submit. Insurers you type are learned for autocompletion."},
gD5(){return"Tools"},
gD6(){return"Ovulation calculator: enter the last cycles (most recent to oldest) to get cycle lengths and the likely ovulation window. Dextograma: gestational calculator by LMP or by first ultrasound."},
gCV(){return"Language"},
gCX(){return"The app detects the system or browser language (Spanish, English, Portuguese, Italian, French or German; if none matches, it uses English). You can set it manually with the globe button in the top bar."},
